; Two libraries, because the rewriter's list of constructor names is data and
; the rewriter is not. A suite has to read that list rather than keep a copy --
; a copy is the failure the list exists to prevent -- and a (kind ppx_rewriter)
; library is not one an ordinary stanza can link: dune builds it for the
; preprocessing context, and `dune build @check`, which is what merlin and the
; language server build, cannot resolve it from a test. Split, the names are an
; ordinary library that anything may name.

(library
 (name camlcast_vocabulary)
 (public_name ppx_camlcast.vocabulary)
 (flags
  (:standard -w +70))
 (modules camlcast_vocabulary))

; The rewriter that tells a description where it was written.
;
; No .mli, and so no -w +70, for the reason demo/ has none: a rewriter is one
; module whose whole interface is a side effect on ppxlib's driver, and an
; interface file for it would restate nothing.
;
; It names ppxlib and nothing of camlcast. It has no need to -- it rewrites
; source text and never links against what that source describes -- and the
; separation is what keeps ppxlib out of camlcast's own dependency list. What
; it emits is a call to Camlcast.Element.at, resolved in the game being
; preprocessed rather than here.

(library
 (name ppx_camlcast)
 (public_name ppx_camlcast)
 (kind ppx_rewriter)
 (modules ppx_camlcast)
 (libraries ppxlib camlcast_vocabulary))
